<title>INDIA: India in $1 bln World Bank talks over Coal India.</title>
<headline>India in $1 bln World Bank talks over Coal India.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Coal Minister Kanti Singh said on Tuesday that the government is in talks with the World Bank to obtain $1 billion for restructuring state-owned Coal India Ltd. </p>
<p>&quot;We are discussing with the World Bank to provide $1 billion for restructuring of CIL (Coal India Ltd),&quot; Singh told a news conference in the Indian capital.</p>
<p>He did not provide any details about the World Bank assistance.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
